      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "I've done a lot of testing of my own on this, and here's what I found on my end.\nAnimating non-humanoid bones on the gesture layer will not work if all of the following are true:\n- The gesture playable layer is using write defaults off\n- The FX playable layer has any states with a motion/animation with write defaults unchecked\n- The layers that contain those state(s) do not have a mask which specifically excludes the bones you want to animate on the gesture layer\nA mask with all humanoid components unchecked without importing the skeleton at all will not work. You have to specifically import the skeleton from your avatar, and uncheck at the least, the bones that you want to animate. Technically unchecking just those bones works but unchecking all of them has no negative side effects, and putting such a mask on all FX layers works as a temporary solution until this behavior is fixed. Leaving the body checked does not cause the issue and so material swaps and similar can still be used without issues. The mask is not needed on the empty default layer in FX. Additionally, the problem will not occur if:\n- The gesture playable layer is using WD on (regardless of whether FX uses WD on or off)\n- Any unmasked layers in the FX playable layer contain only states with WD on, or only empty states, or no states. That is to say, even a combination of masked layers with WD off and unmasked layers with WD on will not cause the issue, though the mixing of WD on and off would likely cause other issues, so this is just an observation to help narrow down the cause.\nThis behavior seems to apply at least all the way back to SDK version 2020.08.06.16.30, which was the oldest one I had saved on my PC. It seems to only be becoming apparent now because of the new Write Defaults off standard, as the issue is not present with a WD on workflow, on any SDK version.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
