      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "I accidentally ran into this issue again and found that if the FX layer mask has at least one transform ticked, you can do material swap animations on the FX layer, but only for material slot 0. (edited for clarity)\nI had an avatar with a bunch of separate meshes with only one material slot each and was animating the materials swaps fine, but when I combined the meshes into one mesh with a bunch of materials and changed the animations, the material swaps stopped working except for the material in slot 0.\nThe behaviour of avatar masks and material swap animations gives me a feeling that this is actually a bug with unity since it can be replicated with a single animation controller with a masked layer containing an animation that swaps materials. The choice of Write Defaults on or Write Defaults off doesn't make a difference.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
