      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "@{58d60ee5acff4444923bdef0|full_name}: I feel like you've missed the point here. The problem was that in order to animate transforms in the Gesture playable layer with Write Defaults Off for all states in both the Gesture playable layer and FX playable layer, it was (and still is) necessary to add an Avatar Mask to every layer in the FX animator controller.\nWhat this leads into is a Unity bug that prevents 'material swap' (material reference) animations from working (aside from slot 0) whenever a layer of an animator controller has an Avatar Mask: https://issuetracker.unity3d.com/issues/avatar-masks-with-non-empty-transforms-prevent-material-reference-animation-of-all-but-material-slot-0\nThis means that users have to make a choice of either having their transform animations in the Gesture playable layer or having fully working 'material swap' animations.\nOtherwise, users must instead either use Write Defaults On, since that does not require adding masks to every layer in the FX animator controller.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
